OL,3,AHow being music's Mr Nice Guy
OL,4,Acontributed to biggest crisis of Ed
OL,5,ASheeran's career
OL,6,
OL,7,FSinger Ed Sheeran is facing the biggest
OL,8,Fcontroversy of his career after a storm
OL,9,Fover a decision to drop support act
OL,10,FMacklemore from his US stadium tour
OL,11,Ffollowing the rapper's on-stage
OL,12,Fpro-Palestinian comments.
OL,14,FSheeran is one of the most successful
OL,15,Fsongwriters of all time. He has sold
OL,16,Fmore than 120 million records and spent
OL,17,Fmore than 1,000 weeks on the US album
OL,18,Fcharts.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/20
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,162,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11911
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1789574061
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AHow being music's Mr Nice Guy
OL,4,Acontributed to biggest crisis of Ed
OL,5,ASheeran's career
OL,6,
OL,7,FPart of his appeal - apart from those
OL,8,Finsidiously catchy songs - is his
OL,9,Feveryman persona. He looks and dresses
OL,10,Flike a fan on the train home from
OL,11,FGlastonbury, rather than one of the
OL,12,Ffestival's headliners.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG11/20
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,162,160,200,105,0,100
